<title>SWEDEN: TABLE - INVESTOR SEES 12-MO 69 PCT RETURN.</title>
<headline>TABLE - INVESTOR SEES 12-MO 69 PCT RETURN.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investor AB, the investment vehicle of Sweden's powerful Wallenberg family, reported for the six months ending June 30 on Thursday. The comparison is to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net worth on June 30 vs Dec 31	  97,316 vs 78,880</p>
<p> Net worth per share on June 30 (SKR)     487 vs    394</p>
<p> Net worth on Aug 4			  99,200 vs 78,880</p>
<p> Net worth per share on Aug 4 (SKR)	 496 vs    394</p>
<p> Value of main holdings June 30	  88,214 vs 61,325</p>
<p> Value of main holdings Aug 4	    90,098 vs 61,325</p>
<p> Total return in yr to June 30 (pct)	 69 vs    n/a</p>
<p> Operating profit			     1,663 vs 11,526*</p>
<p> Net financial items			     41 vs     83*</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		     1,674 vs 11,609*</p>
<p> Tax						  104 vs    122*</p>
<p> Minorities					   8 vs	7*</p>
<p> Consolidated net profit		    1,562 vs 11,480*</p>
<p>NOTE - A * denotes comparison to same 1996 period.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1003</p>
</text>
